# Copy to .env (Bun auto-loads ./.env from this directory on
# `bunx crewhaus run` / `crewhaus dev`). Fill in what you need.

# ── Model (required to RUN the advisor) ───────────────────────────────────
# Either works; ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN takes precedence if both are set.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=...

# ── Thredz = the advisor's brain + dashboard (both specs) ─────────────────
# `thredz:` resolves this at boot (fail-fast, exit 21 when unset) and
# delivers it to the synthesized `npx thredz-mcp` server. Needs a WIKI
# GRANT (read-write or admin): create a key at thredz.crewhaus.ai, then
# grant wiki access via /api/wiki/access.
#
# ONE key for BOTH specs, on purpose. crewhaus.yaml and daemon.yaml declare
# the same `space: trader-advisor`, and an `individual` space is readable
# only by the key that OWNS it — so the shared key is what gives the cli and
# the daemon one brain instead of two. The rule behind that: thredz-mcp
# reads one THREDZ_API_KEY per PROCESS, and a key may own only ONE
# individual space, so per-agent PRIVATE memory means a key per agent and a
# server process per agent. That is the ../expert pattern; this starter
# wants the opposite.
#
# Spaces need Pro or Scale (Pro: 5 shared / 10 individual across ≤10 keys;
# Scale: 25 / 50 across ≤50 keys). Free and Starter have no spaces at all —
# there, delete `space:` from both specs and the advisor uses the unspaced
# legacy wiki exactly as it did before 0.5.0.
#
# Create the space before the first run — over the Thredz API, or by asking
# the advisor once ("create an individual wiki space trader-advisor"); its
# wiki_space_create call is justification-gated, so you approve it. If the
# slug names no space the key can reach, the wiki calls fail per call (the
# run degrades to clear errors; it does not crash the harness).
THREDZ_API_KEY=
# Self-hosted / local Thredz? Use base_url in the spec's thredz: block.

# ── Web research (required for /study and heartbeat STUDY) ────────────────
CREWHAUS_SEARCH_PROVIDER=
CREWHAUS_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# ── Slack (only for daemon.yaml) ──────────────────────────────────────────
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ── Paper broker tuning (all optional; defaults shown) ────────────────────
# Fee rates carry effective dates and change — see
# sources/costs-and-constraints.md before overriding.
# PAPER_SEED_USD=5000
# PAPER_HALF_SPREAD_BPS=3
# PAPER_SLIPPAGE_BPS=2
# PAPER_CRYPTO_FEE_BPS=60
# PAPER_CRYPTO_SPREAD_BPS=10
# PAPER_SEC_FEE_PER_M=20.60
# PAPER_TAF_PER_SHARE=0.000195
# PAPER_TAF_CAP=9.79
# PAPER_RISK_PCT=0.01
# PAPER_MAX_POS_PCT=0.20
# PAPER_HALT_PCT=0.15
# CONFIDENCE_MIN_TRADES=40
# CONFIDENCE_MIN_PF=1.3
# CONFIDENCE_MAX_DD=0.15
